SUMMARY:Tal Naccarato\, LIVE!\, Unplugged!
DESCRIPTION:Guitarist / Songwriter and Instrumentalist in the  Americana / 
 Folk- Blues tradition performs Solo Acoustic from his original and 
 traditional repertoire and discusses and demonstrates the history of this 
 particular musical genre while exhibiting\,  performing on and displaying 
 rare vintage period instruments during the course of a live musical 
 concert.\n\n\n\nShort Bio:\n\nTal Naccarato is a dynamic composer\, 
 songwriter and teacher artist whose roots stretch from the medieval 
 mountain village of Fiumefreddo Bruzio\, Italy\, to the heart of East 
 Flatbush\, Brooklyn. His original music fuses Folk\, Americana\, Rock\, and 
 Blues with classical guitar flair and a signature bluesy swing. In 2023\, 
 Tal took home top honors at the Long Island Blues Society Solo/Duo 
 Competition. Tal performs solo acoustic from his original and traditional 
 repertoire. Everyone is welcome. \n\nCoffee and light refreshments will be 
 served.
LOCATION:Nutley - Children's Room\, Nutley Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Nutley Library":MAILTO:events@nutley.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:
