BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260627T180000Z
DTEND:20260627T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260627T000000Z
SUMMARY:Michelle Cray - Stretched Book Discussion and Signing.
DESCRIPTION: \n\nMichelle must face the harsh reality of her childhood in 
 order to overcome the pain that has long held her captive. From the time 
 she was five years old\, when she witnessed the near-death experience of 
 her sister\, her world was shaped by trauma. Her mother struggled with 
 mental illness\, she was abandoned by those she loved\, and she was scarred 
 by sexual assault\, carrying the wounds of her past into every relationship 
 she formed as an adult.\n\nStretched follows Michelle’s true story 
 through the long aftermath of trauma\, and how early abandonment and 
 violence seep into identity\, self-worth\, and the choices she made. 
 Similar to The Glass Castle and Educated\, her memoir depicts how hope can 
 thrive in the face of incredible hardship\, how pain can be transformed 
 into resilience\, and how forgiveness can free oneself of the burdens that 
 lie within.\n\nAbout Michelle:\nHi! I’m Michelle Cray\, mother of two 
 boys and author of my memoir\, Stretched\, and my comedic novella\, Not 
 About Him. I grew up in Nutley\, a small town in northern New Jersey. When 
 I turned 18\, I left home to attend Syracuse University and pursue a degree 
 in finance. Life in the corporate world worked out for me for a solid 
 fifteen years\, until 2020 when the world shut down and I gave birth to my 
 first son. At that point\, I found greater joy in raising a family and was 
 lucky enough to be able to quit my job and start my career as an author.
LOCATION:Nutley - Stockton Room\, Nutley Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Nutley Library":MAILTO:events@nutley.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-10315-16202408
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16202408
