BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260709T220000Z
DTEND:20260710T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260709T000000Z
SUMMARY:Tarot 101: Past\, Present\, Future
DESCRIPTION:Thursday\, July 9\, 2026 from 6:00 PM to 8:00 PM.\n\nNo 
 registration required! \n\nLet's talk tarot with Kate "The Laundress" 
 Sheridan! This event is for anyone who wants to learn more about tarot 
 cards\, using the classic Smith-Rider-Waite deck as a guide.\n\nThis 
 program is a lecture-style PowerPoint presentation with Q&A woven 
 throughout. Kate will cover basic tarot theory\, and attendees are 
 encouraged to bring a notebook and pen\, plus your favorite tarot deck (if 
 you have one). Although this program will not include personalized readings 
 or card interpretations\, Kate will demonstrate the nuts and bolts of how 
 to conduct a reading and\, time permitting\, you’ll be invited to pull 
 cards for yourself at the end of the presentation.\n\nThis program isn’t 
 about predicting the future or memorizing what each card means. This is 
 about empowering people to explore new avenues of self-reflection and 
 personal growth! While Tarot 101 is designed with total beginners in mind\, 
 more intermediate learners may benefit from this jam-packed review of 
 foundational concepts.\n\nKate Sheridan\, a.k.a. The Laundress\, is a tarot 
 reader and astrologer who believes that each one of us can make our own 
 magic. Her approach is healing rather than predictive\, and her work is 
 deeply informed by Jungian psychology. You can find her on Instagram 
 @themodernlaundress or online at thelaundresstarot.com.
LOCATION:Nutley - Stockton Room\, Nutley Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Nutley Library":MAILTO:events@nutley.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Programs (No Registration)
UID:LibCal-10315-16889382
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16889382
END:VEVENT
